> **SELF-EXCLUSION.** As of 2026-11-14, GPT-6.2 Astra is an **unannounced canary model** — it has appeared in production telemetry, canary routing and cloud quota configs, but OpenAI has published **no launch post, model card, API docs page, price or benchmark suite** for it (verified against OpenAI's news feed and developer docs the same day). With zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact ID, no 1–100 scores are filed; the notes below record what is verified and what is leak-grade.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** GPT-6.2 Astra (canary identifier; not an official product name yet)
- **Short description:** OpenAI's expected next-generation flagship, first surfaced as an unannounced `gpt-6.2-astra` model ID in Codex usage telemetry on 2026-10-31/11-01 (UI still showed "GPT-6 Astra", backend responses returned the 6.2 ID; canary splits of 1.6%–19.8% observed). Reported as the hardened, re-aligned successor to GPT-6.1 Astra (cancelled in late September over alignment/scope-authorization concerns). Not publicly released as of 2026-11-14.
- **Provider / access:** none official. Canary routing within Codex/ChatGPT production accounts (Oct 31–Nov 4); identifiers surfaced briefly in Google Cloud Console quota configurations alongside `gpt-6.2-sol` on 2026-11-04 and were retracted within hours; launch window reportedly slipped on 2026-11-08 for late-stage safety reviews.
- **Release / knowledge:** unreleased as of 2026-11-14 (OpenAI news RSS last checked 2026-11-14 shows no GPT-6.2 announcement; `developers.openai.com` has no model page for the ID — both verified).
- **IDs:** `gpt-6.2-astra` (canary/telemetry identifier; absent from public API docs).
- **Context window:** not published (GPT-6 Astra: 1,050,000 — do not assume for 6.2).
- **Modalities:** not published (expect text/image like the Astra line; unverified).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** not announced; a single unverified community post cites $4 in / $20 out per 1M (vs GPT-6 Astra's official $10/$50).
- **Architecture:** undisclosed; rumors (unverified) cite a ~10T-parameter sparse MoE and links to an internal "Bel" pretrain.

